        "original_id": "3cc83c0b-ef6a-56e9-a64f-3ea2c1c1f5f1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Shaheed Udham Singh\n- People: Udham Singh, Michael O'Dwyer, Reginald Dyer\n- Events: Jallianwala Bagh massacre\n- Places: Jallianwala Bagh, Amritsar, Punjab\n- Organizations: British Indian Army\n- Roles: Lieutenant Governor of the Punjab\n\nFacts:\n- On 13 April 1919, the Jallianwala Bagh massacre, also called the Amritsar massacre, took place at Jallianwala Bagh in Amritsar, Punjab.\n- On 13 April 1919, troops of the British Indian Army under Colonel Reginald Dyer fired on a crowd of non-violent protesters and Baishakhi pilgrims gathered at Jallianwala Bagh.\n- Michael O'Dwyer was the British Lieutenant Governor of the Punjab and is described here as having ordered the Jallianwala Bagh massacre.\n- Udham Singh is described here as having devoted his life to punishing Michael O'Dwyer.\n- Shaheed Udham Singh is a 2000 revolutionary film based on the life of Udham Singh.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
